1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:03,080
Hi,  and  welcome  back  to  Act.  You

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,759
already  have  a  clear  problem  in

3
00:00:04,759 --> 00:00:06,839
front  of  you.  Now  comes  a  very

4
00:00:06,839 --> 00:00:08,760
important  question.  What  do  the

5
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,440
people  affected  by  this  problem

6
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,120
actually  need?

7
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:13,679
It  sounds  simple,  but  this  is

8
00:00:13,679 --> 00:00:15,719
where  many  projects  go  wrong.

9
00:00:15,719 --> 00:00:17,160
People  often  choose  a  solution

10
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:19,279
because  it  looks  useful,  modern,

11
00:00:19,279 --> 00:00:21,480
or  easy  to  organize.  But  a  good

12
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,080
solution  should  come  after  the

13
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:25,640
need,  not  before  it.  So  for  now,

14
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:27,920
forget  about  apps,  campaigns,

15
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:30,039
workshops,  donations,  or  any  other

16
00:00:30,039 --> 00:00:33,079
idea.  Focus  on  the  people.  What

17
00:00:33,079 --> 00:00:34,800
are  they  struggling  with?  What  is

18
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,520
stopping  them?  And  what  kind  of

19
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:37,719
help  would  really  make  a

20
00:00:37,719 --> 00:00:38,583
difference?

21
00:00:38,583 --> 00:00:40,422
Let's  make  this  easier  with  a

22
00:00:40,422 --> 00:00:42,942
simple  example.  Think  about  four

23
00:00:42,942 --> 00:00:45,823
very  different  cases.  A  tree,  a

24
00:00:45,823 --> 00:00:48,903
student,  a  horse,  and  a  carpenter.

25
00:00:48,903 --> 00:00:51,543
What  does  each  one  need  to  grow,

26
00:00:51,543 --> 00:00:55,743
learn,  move,  or  do  the  job  well?

27
00:00:55,743 --> 00:00:57,583
The  answers  will  be  different

28
00:00:57,583 --> 00:00:58,983
because  their  situations  are

29
00:00:58,983 --> 00:01:00,063
different.

30
00:01:00,063 --> 00:01:02,063
A  hammer  may  help  a  carpenter,

31
00:01:02,063 --> 00:01:04,423
but  it  is  useless  to  a  horse.

32
00:01:04,423 --> 00:01:06,543
A  notebook  may  help  a  student,

33
00:01:06,543 --> 00:01:07,903
but  it  will  not  help  a  tree

34
00:01:07,903 --> 00:01:09,063
grow.

35
00:01:09,063 --> 00:01:11,223
This  sounds  obvious,  right?  But

36
00:01:11,223 --> 00:01:12,822
the  same  mistake  happens  in

37
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:14,583
community  projects.

38
00:01:14,583 --> 00:01:16,383
We  sometimes  give  people  the  tool

39
00:01:16,383 --> 00:01:18,343
we  like,  instead  of  the  support

40
00:01:18,343 --> 00:01:20,103
they  really  need.

41
00:01:20,103 --> 00:01:21,982
The  first  job  is  to  understand

42
00:01:21,982 --> 00:01:24,083
the  person  and  the  situation.

43
00:01:24,323 --> 00:01:27,242
So,  what  do  we  mean  by  a  need?

44
00:01:27,242 --> 00:01:29,323
Keep  it  simple.  A  need  is

45
00:01:29,323 --> 00:01:30,922
something  important  that  helps  a

46
00:01:30,922 --> 00:01:32,883
person  or  group  improve  their

47
00:01:32,883 --> 00:01:34,123
situation.

48
00:01:34,123 --> 00:01:36,682
It  could  be  information,  a  skill,

49
00:01:36,682 --> 00:01:39,163
transport,  equipment,  access  to  a

50
00:01:39,163 --> 00:01:41,883
service,  time,  support,  or

51
00:01:41,883 --> 00:01:43,323
something  else.

52
00:01:43,323 --> 00:01:44,923
The  important  part  is  that  the

53
00:01:44,923 --> 00:01:46,563
need  should  come  from  the  real

54
00:01:46,563 --> 00:01:49,323
problem,  not  from  our  guess.

55
00:01:49,323 --> 00:01:51,282
For  example,  if  someone  cannot  use

56
00:01:51,282 --> 00:01:53,563
a  service,  the  real  need  may  not

57
00:01:53,563 --> 00:01:55,362
be  “a  new  app.”

58
00:01:55,362 --> 00:01:56,723
Maybe  the  problem  is  that  they  do

59
00:01:56,723 --> 00:01:58,683
not  know  the  service  exists,

60
00:01:58,683 --> 00:02:00,322
cannot  reach  it,  or  do  not

61
00:02:00,322 --> 00:02:02,603
understand  how  to  use  it.

62
00:02:02,603 --> 00:02:04,443
Different  causes  can  create  very

63
00:02:04,443 --> 00:02:06,083
different  needs,  even  when  the

64
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:07,403
problem  looks  similar  from  the

65
00:02:07,403 --> 00:02:08,208
outside.

66
00:02:08,208 --> 00:02:10,808
Go  back  to  the  issue  you  chose.

67
00:02:10,808 --> 00:02:13,328
Ask  yourself  four  questions.  Who

68
00:02:13,328 --> 00:02:15,368
is  affected  most?  What  are  they

69
00:02:15,368 --> 00:02:18,488
unable  to  do,  get  or  reach?  What

70
00:02:18,488 --> 00:02:20,608
seems  to  be  stopping  them  and

71
00:02:20,608 --> 00:02:23,128
what  kind  of  support  could  help?

72
00:02:23,128 --> 00:02:25,407
Do  not  rush  the  answers.

73
00:02:25,407 --> 00:02:26,808
Use  the  information  you  collected

74
00:02:26,808 --> 00:02:28,768
before  and  pay  attention  to  what

75
00:02:28,768 --> 00:02:31,807
people  actually  say  or  experience.

76
00:02:31,807 --> 00:02:33,288
Sometimes  the  people  living  with

77
00:02:33,288 --> 00:02:34,487
the  problem  will  point  out

78
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:36,688
something  you  completely  missed.

79
00:02:36,688 --> 00:02:39,048
That  is  useful. You  are  not  trying

80
00:02:39,048 --> 00:02:40,807
to  prove  that  your  first  idea  was

81
00:02:40,807 --> 00:02:42,447
correct.  You  are  trying  to

82
00:02:42,447 --> 00:02:44,927
understand  the  situation  better.

83
00:02:44,927 --> 00:02:47,048
The  clearer  the  need  becomes,  the

84
00:02:47,048 --> 00:02:48,528
easier  it  will  be  to  choose  a

85
00:02:48,528 --> 00:02:50,708
solution  that  actually  fits.

86
00:02:50,948 --> 00:02:53,148
Here  is  a  quick  test.  Imagine  the

87
00:02:53,148 --> 00:02:54,788
people  you  want  to  help  need

88
00:02:54,788 --> 00:02:56,668
training,  but  you  only  give  them

89
00:02:56,668 --> 00:02:58,908
equipment.  The  equipment  may  sit

90
00:02:58,908 --> 00:03:01,028
there  unused,  or  maybe  they

91
00:03:01,028 --> 00:03:02,708
already  have  the  knowledge,  but

92
00:03:02,708 --> 00:03:05,108
the  real  problem  is  transport.

93
00:03:05,108 --> 00:03:06,788
Giving  them  more  information  will

94
00:03:06,788 --> 00:03:09,508
not  fix  that.  A  project  can  look

95
00:03:09,508 --> 00:03:11,468
good  and  still  miss  the  real

96
00:03:11,468 --> 00:03:14,307
need.  That  is  why  helping  is  not

97
00:03:14,307 --> 00:03:16,348
only  about  doing  something.  It  is

98
00:03:16,348 --> 00:03:18,708
about  doing  something  that  fits.

99
00:03:18,708 --> 00:03:20,747
Sometimes  the  best  support  is  very

100
00:03:20,747 --> 00:03:23,628
simple.  Sometimes  it  is  not.

101
00:03:23,628 --> 00:03:25,988
The  question  is  always  the  same.

102
00:03:25,988 --> 00:03:27,628
Does  this  really  help  with  the

103
00:03:27,628 --> 00:03:29,828
barrier  people  are  facing?  Or  are

104
00:03:29,828 --> 00:03:30,988
we  just  giving  them  what  is

105
00:03:30,988 --> 00:03:32,708
easiest  for  us  to  provide?

106
00:03:32,708 --> 00:03:34,908
Now,  let's  try  it  with  your  own

107
00:03:34,908 --> 00:03:37,788
issue.  Finish  this  sentence.

108
00:03:37,788 --> 00:03:39,627
The  people  affected  by  this  issue

109
00:03:39,627 --> 00:03:41,267
need?

110
00:03:41,267 --> 00:03:43,347
Write  one  answer,  then  look  at  it

111
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:44,307
again.

112
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:46,068
Is  it  a  need  or  did  you

113
00:03:46,068 --> 00:03:48,227
accidentally  write  a  solution?

114
00:03:48,227 --> 00:03:50,708
For  example,  they  need  an  app  is

115
00:03:50,708 --> 00:03:52,428
already  a  solution.

116
00:03:52,428 --> 00:03:53,747
Ask  yourself  what  the  app  is

117
00:03:53,747 --> 00:03:55,668
supposed  to  help  them  do.

118
00:03:55,668 --> 00:03:57,508
Maybe  the  real  need  is  easier

119
00:03:57,508 --> 00:03:59,508
access  to  information,  faster

120
00:03:59,508 --> 00:04:01,668
communication  or  a  simpler  way  to

121
00:04:01,668 --> 00:04:03,708
complete  a  task.

122
00:04:03,708 --> 00:04:05,427
When  you  find  the  need  behind  the

123
00:04:05,427 --> 00:04:07,228
solution,  you  open  the  door  to

124
00:04:07,228 --> 00:04:09,508
more  than  one  possible  answer.

125
00:04:09,508 --> 00:04:11,228
That  gives  you  more  freedom  later

126
00:04:11,228 --> 00:04:12,587
because  you  can  compare  different

127
00:04:12,587 --> 00:04:14,188
ways  to  help  instead  of  getting

128
00:04:14,188 --> 00:04:16,416
stuck  on  one  idea  too  early.

129
00:04:16,416 --> 00:04:19,216
Now,  compare  your  problem  sentence

130
00:04:19,216 --> 00:04:21,175
with  your  need  sentence.  They

131
00:04:21,175 --> 00:04:22,576
should  connect,  but  they  should

132
00:04:22,576 --> 00:04:24,736
not  say  the  same  thing.

133
00:04:24,736 --> 00:04:26,376
The  problem  tells  you  what  is

134
00:04:26,376 --> 00:04:28,656
going  wrong.  The  need  tells  you

135
00:04:28,656 --> 00:04:29,896
what  could  help  the  people

136
00:04:29,896 --> 00:04:32,775
affected  move  forward.

137
00:04:32,775 --> 00:04:34,535
If  the  problem  is  clear,  but  the

138
00:04:34,535 --> 00:04:36,736
need  still  feels  weak,  that  is

139
00:04:36,736 --> 00:04:38,976
okay.  Go  back  and  learn  a  little

140
00:04:38,976 --> 00:04:40,296
more.

141
00:04:40,296 --> 00:04:41,976
If  the  need  does  not  clearly

142
00:04:41,976 --> 00:04:43,736
connect  to  the  problem,  check  it

143
00:04:43,736 --> 00:04:44,896
again.

144
00:04:44,896 --> 00:04:46,455
There  is  no  prize  for  moving

145
00:04:46,455 --> 00:04:49,015
fast.  Taking  extra  time  here  can

146
00:04:49,015 --> 00:04:50,696
save  you  from  building  the  wrong

147
00:04:50,696 --> 00:04:52,616
thing  later.

148
00:04:52,616 --> 00:04:54,495
Good  community  work  is  not  about

149
00:04:54,495 --> 00:04:56,536
having  the  quickest  answer.  It  is

150
00:04:56,536 --> 00:04:57,936
about  choosing  an  answer  that

151
00:04:57,936 --> 00:04:59,576
makes  sense  for  the  people  you

152
00:04:59,576 --> 00:05:00,916
want  to  support.

153
00:05:00,916 --> 00:05:03,156
Before  you  finish,  keep  three

154
00:05:03,156 --> 00:05:05,116
things  together.  Your  problem

155
00:05:05,116 --> 00:05:07,195
statement,  the  useful  information

156
00:05:07,195 --> 00:05:09,156
you  found  and  your  current  need

157
00:05:09,156 --> 00:05:10,435
statement.

158
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:12,276
You  may  still  improve  them  later

159
00:05:12,276 --> 00:05:14,156
and  that  is  normal.

160
00:05:14,156 --> 00:05:17,275
For  now,  the  main  idea  is  simple.

161
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:19,275
Different  people  and  situations

162
00:05:19,275 --> 00:05:21,396
need  different  kinds  of  support

163
00:05:21,396 --> 00:05:23,355
and  the  right  tool  only  works

164
00:05:23,355 --> 00:05:26,316
when  it  matches  the  real  need.

165
00:05:26,316 --> 00:05:28,076
Next,  we  can  finally  start

166
00:05:28,076 --> 00:05:29,876
thinking  about  solutions.

167
00:05:29,876 --> 00:05:31,595
But  instead  of choosing  the  first

168
00:05:31,595 --> 00:05:33,396
idea  that  comes  to  mind,  we  are

169
00:05:33,396 --> 00:05:35,196
going  to  create  several  options

170
00:05:35,196 --> 00:05:36,196
first.

171
00:05:36,196 --> 00:05:37,436
That  gives  you  a  much  better

172
00:05:37,436 --> 00:05:38,596
chance  of  finding  something

173
00:05:38,596 --> 00:05:40,795
practical,  useful  and  worth

174
00:05:40,795 --> 00:05:42,276
developing.

175
00:05:42,276 --> 00:05:44,036
That's  it  for  today.  Keep  your

176
00:05:44,036 --> 00:05:45,436
notes  with  you  and  I'll  see  you

177
00:05:45,436 --> 00:05:46,624
in  the  next  lesson.
